    "['controller E1 [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set interfaces e1-1/0/0 controller-type e1', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'set interfaces e1-1/0/0 controller-type e1', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': '##\\nset interfaces e1-1/0/0 controller-type e1\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n- In Juniper, E1 controller configuration is set under the interface hierarchy.\\n- The command specifies the interface (e1-1/0/0) and sets the controller type to E1.\\n- This is the Juniper equivalent of Huawei\\'s \"controller E1 1/0/0\" command that establishes the physical interface as an E1 controller.', 'trans_template': 'set interfaces e1-1/0/0 controller-type e1'}]]": 1,
    "['using e1', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set interfaces ct1-1/0/0 framing e1', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces e1-1/0/0 controller-type e1'], 'root': 'set interfaces e1-1/0/0 controller-type e1', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"##\\nset interfaces ct1-1/0/0 framing e1\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n- In Juniper, E1 configuration is typically done under the `ct1` (Channelized T1/E1) interface.\\n- The `using e1` command in Huawei specifies E1 framing mode, which is equivalent to `framing e1` in Juniper.\\n- The interface naming follows Juniper's format where `ct1-1/0/0` corresponds to the physical slot location (1/0/0 in Huawei).\", 'trans_template': 'set interfaces ct1-1/0/0 framing e1'}]]": 1,
