    "['cable-length [parameter1] [parameter2]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set interfaces e1-1/0/0 attenuation 0', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces e1-1/0/0 controller-type e1'], 'root': 'set interfaces e1-1/0/0 controller-type e1', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'The equivalent Juniper command for `cable-length long 0db` would be configuring the E1 line attenuation. Here\\'s the translation:\\n\\n##\\nset interfaces e1-1/0/0 attenuation 0\\n##\\n\\nThis sets the attenuation level to 0 dB for the E1 interface, which matches the \"long 0db\" cable-length specification in the Huawei configuration. Note that Juniper uses \"attenuation\" rather than \"cable-length\" as the parameter name.', 'trans_template': 'set interfaces e1-1/0/0 attenuation 0'}]]": 1,
    "['mp-group [parameter1] timeslot [parameter2]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set interfaces ct1-1/0/0 timeslots 1-31', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces e1-1/0/0 controller-type e1'], 'root': 'set interfaces e1-1/0/0 controller-type e1', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here’s the equivalent Juniper configuration command for the HUAWEI `mp-group 1 timeslot 1-31` command:\\n\\n##\\nset interfaces ct1-1/0/0 timeslots 1-31\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n- In Juniper, `ct1-1/0/0` represents the T1/E1 controller interface (similar to HUAWEI's `E1 1/0/0`).\\n- The `timeslots 1-31` directive is used similarly in Juniper to assign all timeslots (equivalent to HUAWEI's command).\\n- Note that Juniper typically uses a different syntax structure for bundling (e.g., multilink PPP would be configured separately under interface options).\", 'trans_template': 'set interfaces ct1-1/0/0 timeslots 1-31'}]]": 1,
